From 6b9acaedb5a4c51a93349a1d9c5a0c07d59d91e9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: orca-kobra <orca-kobra@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 24 Sep 2026 20:59:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 2/4] plugin host: expose per-filament slice statistics

Add orca.host.slice_statistics(plate_index=-1). It returns the per-filament
volumes of a plate's last valid slice (model, support, prime tower, flush,
total in mm^3) together with filament diameter and density, taken from the
same GCodeProcessor statistics the preview legend uses, and the filament
changes in order: "transitions" lists each (from, to) pair with its count,
from None for the first filament.

Plugins can use it to compare a slice with what is left on the loaded spools,
and to estimate a filament changer's purge per colour change. The plate's
slice result is now marked valid before SlicingJobComplete is fired, so a
handler of that event can read it.
